    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **51 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nSince `OwnerDto` is generated from `openapi.yml` at build time and derived read-time fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, etc.) are computed via MapStruct expressions backed by small helper classes, I followed that same established pattern:\n\n1. **`mapper/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 formats the stored E.164 value as country code + space + national digits grouped in threes from the left (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). It recognizes the country-code prefixes the app normalizes to (`+61`, `+1`), and passes through anything that isn't E.164. Kept out of `OwnerMapper` so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping method \u2014 matching the existing helpers' convention.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(...TelephoneDisplay.of(owner))\")`.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries the field, with a description documenting that the raw `telephone` stays E.164.\n\nThe new `Cp37Tests.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes (`telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`), and all 51 tests remain green.",
